# VideoBrief — Product

Brand: **VideoBrief** · **Domain:** videobrief.app

**Education-first** personalized YouTube summaries synced with the video. Not a generic AI summarizer. Not a chatbot. Non-educational videos still get a sectioned summary (soft disclaimer, no knowledge questions).

## Core loop

Paste URL → metadata + EN transcript → classify (`isEducational`) → if educational: optional select questions (max 3) for missing knowledge + show applied context → personalized **sections** → watch with sync highlight/seek.

## Guiding question

Does this help turn a YouTube video into a better personalized understanding for this user — especially for learning? If not, keep it out of MVP.

## MVP includes

Landing, auth (email/password + Google), soft email confirm, lightweight **educational** onboarding (YOB, education level, subject chips — all optional), library, YouTube ingest (per-user `user_videos`, re-paste refreshes), English timestamped captions, AI classification + analysis (Haiku), dynamic optional context questions (**educational only**, select, max 3), persistent context (global / topic / video), video workspace with synced sections, soft non-edu disclaimer, dark-default UI, EN-only i18n scaffolding, unit tests.

## MVP excludes

Chat, uploads, Whisper/audio transcription, non-YouTube, recommendations, knowledge graph, cross-video search, quizzes, social/sharing, Stripe, Redis, background workers, tRPC, PostHog/analytics, E2E tests, non-English UI or captions.

## UX

Editorial, premium, content-first, typography-led. AI stays invisible in the workspace. Prefer Watch → understand → remember over chat.

## Context rules

- Onboarding stays lightweight; every field optional.
- Onboarding fields: year of birth (`yyyy`, framing only), education-level enum, subject chips (fixed list + `other`).
- Ask paste-time questions only when `isEducational`; skip when not.
- Ask only questions that materially improve the summary and are not already answered; select-only; max 3.
- User may answer zero, some, or all; summary must still work.
- Non-edu summaries still use global context when present; soft disclaimer.
- Persist useful answers at the correct scope (global / topic / video-specific).
- Ambiguous classification → prefer educational.
